{"parentUuid":"6fa2c182-1713-4116-a124-bc53c6261d8d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxGj3iTxW5XNt9dpDAAR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TXYcEohHxShcB3hQ651UZH","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"npx vitest run cli/site-frames.test.ts 2>&1 | grep -E \"×|Tests\"; git add -A site && git commit -qm \"feat(site): measured comparison with its limits, second cap-and-escalate proof\" && perl -e 'alarm 110; exec @ARGV' git push -q -u origin HEAD 2>&1 | tail -1; gh pr create --base main --title \"feat(site): measured comparison and second cap-and-escalate proof\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n- **Judges, 30%:** new card \"Measured: the same three tasks, with and without Tally\": the agreed sentence, three bars ($1.22, $0.31, $0.43) with per-task costs, tiers and \"3 of 3 passed\", and the limits printed beside it (three tasks, one run each; list-price estimates; the trace-history pass was not cheaper; trace history changed one estimate and no tier or ceiling; cfo.ai off). No single savings percentage.\n- One limit added from the ledgers themselves: in all three passes each task's first start failed before using tokens and was retried at $0.00.\n- **Near \"What Tally does\":** the same comparison as a compact three-bar figure with sample size and a link to the full numbers.\n- **Cap and escalate:** `run-20261012-100856Z` on fly-doom-jev is now the lead (stopped at $0.0196 against $0.018, escalated on the same branch, middle tier passed at $0.170, Tally opened PR #17 unattended); the earlier forced-stop run is kept in the note.\n- \"Measured baseline saving\" is no longer an empty slot. Version stays 0.1.0.\n\n## Tests\nPer-task and total costs checked by me against the three ledgers in `comparison-runs/` (A $1.2169, B $0.3093, C $0.4263). `cli/site-frames.test.ts` passes. Looked at in headless Chrome at 1440 px. The escalation run's figures are as supplied; I confirmed only that fly-doom-jev PR #17 exists and is open.\n\n## After merge\nRedeploy with `vercel deploy --prod` from `site/`.\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Commit, push and open the PR","timeout":200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2892,"cache_read_input_tokens":780991,"output_tokens":902,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2892,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":902,"cache_read_input_tokens":780991,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2892,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2892},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TXYcEohHxShcB3hQ651UZH":{"command":"cd /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-6 && npx vitest run cli/site-frames.test.ts 2>&1 | grep -E \"×|Tests\"; git add -A site && git commit -qm \"feat(site): measured comparison with its limits, second cap-and-escalate proof\" && perl -e 'alarm 110; exec @ARGV' git push -q -u origin HEAD 2>&1 | tail -1; gh pr create --base main --title \"feat(site): measured comparison and second cap-and-escalate proof\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n- **Judges, 30%:** new card \"Measured: the same three tasks, with and without Tally\": the agreed sentence, three bars ($1.22, $0.31, $0.43) with per-task costs, tiers and \"3 of 3 passed\", and the limits printed beside it (three tasks, one run each; list-price estimates; the trace-history pass was not cheaper; trace history changed one estimate and no tier or ceiling; cfo.ai off). No single savings percentage.\n- One limit added from the ledgers themselves: in all three passes each task's first start failed before using tokens and was retried at $0.00.\n- **Near \"What Tally does\":** the same comparison as a compact three-bar figure with sample size and a link to the full numbers.\n- **Cap and escalate:** `run-20261012-100856Z` on fly-doom-jev is now the lead (stopped at $0.0196 against $0.018, escalated on the same branch, middle tier passed at $0.170, Tally opened PR #17 unattended); the earlier forced-stop run is kept in the note.\n- \"Measured baseline saving\" is no longer an empty slot. Version stays 0.1.0.\n\n## Tests\nPer-task and total costs checked by me against the three ledgers in `comparison-runs/` (A $1.2169, B $0.3093, C $0.4263). `cli/site-frames.test.ts` passes. Looked at in headless Chrome at 1440 px. The escalation run's figures are as supplied; I confirmed only that fly-doom-jev PR #17 exists and is open.\n\n## After merge\nRedeploy with `vercel deploy --prod` from `site/`.\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Commit, push and open the PR","timeout":200000}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01TXYcEohHxShcB3hQ651UZH":{"cwd":"/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-6"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"25e6d089-57f3-42fa-9bef-e4de7bce3c95","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfxGe25bWjW6CaZkX2wUf","type":"assistant","uuid":"dde04e12-b361-4ef0-b4e3-40fc0ff8eee4","timestamp":"2026-10-12T11:34:27.563Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","perTurnEffort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-6","sessionId":"62bf8255-2828-4016-bc6c-8d8c4893b1a2","version":"2.1.287","gitBranch":"ao/neatlogs-hack-6/site-comparison"}
