{"parentUuid":"ab5a6961-5468-47eb-8ffd-606b04ada13e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxGyk9D6Vgabic31H2Wc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AujnSvmizH68UqV2PHvHq8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"URL=$(gh pr create --base main --title \"feat(site): measured comparison and second cap-and-escalate proof\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n- **Judges, 30%:** new card \"Measured: the same three tasks, with and without Tally\": the agreed sentence, three bars ($1.22, $0.31, $0.43) with per-task costs, tiers and \"3 of 3 passed\", and the limits printed beside it (three tasks, one run each; list-price estimates; the trace-history pass was not cheaper; trace history changed one estimate and no tier or ceiling; cfo.ai off). No single savings percentage.\n- One limit added from the ledgers themselves: in all three passes each task's first start failed before using tokens and was retried at $0.00.\n- **Near \"What Tally does\":** the same comparison as a compact three-bar figure with sample size and a link to the full numbers.\n- **Cap and escalate:** `run-20261012-100856Z` on fly-doom-jev is now the lead (stopped at $0.0196 against $0.018, escalated on the same branch, middle tier passed at $0.170, Tally opened PR #17 unattended); the earlier forced-stop run is kept in the note.\n- \"Measured baseline saving\" is no longer an empty slot. Version stays 0.1.0.\n\n## Tests\nPer-task and total costs checked against the three ledgers in `comparison-runs/` (A $1.2169, B $0.3093, C $0.4263). `cli/site-frames.test.ts` passes. Looked at in headless Chrome at 1440 px only. The escalation run's figures are as supplied; I confirmed only that fly-doom-jev PR #17 exists and is open.\n\n## After merge\nRedeploy with `vercel deploy --prod` from `site/`.\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1); echo $URL; ao send --session neatlogs-hack-8 --message \"Lane C: PR open from 6196474: $URL . Judges 30% now has the measured comparison with your sentence, three bars (\\$1.22, \\$0.31, \\$0.43), per-task costs and tiers, 3 of 3 each, and every limit you listed printed beside it; no savings percentage. I checked the per-task and total figures against the three ledgers myself. One limit I added because the ledgers show it: in all three passes each task's first start failed with 'worker never started' at \\$0.00 and was retried; say if you want that line removed. A compact three-bar version sits under the five steps with the sample size and a link to the full card. Cap-and-escalate now leads with run-20261012-100856Z (\\$0.0196 against \\$0.018, same branch, middle passed at \\$0.170, PR #17 unattended) and keeps the earlier run in a note; I verified only that PR #17 exists and is open, the figures are yours. The 'measured baseline saving' empty slot is gone; the only empty slots left are the #neatHack links and the public link to the cfo.ai plan. Version stays 0.1.0. Not checked: phone width for the new card was captured but not looked at closely; headless Chrome only. Tell me when merged and I will redeploy and confirm the live text.\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Open the PR and tell the orchestrator","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":368,"cache_read_input_tokens":784875,"output_tokens":1217,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":368,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1217,"cache_read_input_tokens":784875,"cache_creation_input_tokens":368,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":368},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null